    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e488f176_8cae2aee",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 382,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T15:43:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if this identifies the host?\n\nAddituionally, do we need to prevent the host from spoofing these messages?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 382,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 382,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ea7019b_23d7b2d0",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 382,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T04:22:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Linux driver first calls `RXTX_MAP`, then `PARTITION_INFO_GET` (which makes sense because the information goes in the RX buffer), including on the host.\n\nThis means that we\u0027ll never see the host here because `sp_ids` will be empty here. Is that intended?",
      "parentUuid": "e488f176_8cae2aee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 382,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 382,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c10a7ee4_f46b0e8e",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 382,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-09T01:49:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "1ea7019b_23d7b2d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 382,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 382,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "feec5b27_002c75a5",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 384,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T15:43:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hrm, maybe we should only send the notification if the rxtx_map operation actually succeeds?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 384,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 384,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "146325ce_277ba84d",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 384,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-19T00:42:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the VM creation message needs to be sent long before this point. The VM creation message has response status codes that tells the caller it needs to resend the message. RXTX_MAP does not have that, so I don\u0027t think you can handle this in this context. Also, if you delay sending the VM creation message until RXTX_MAP is called, then you need to make sure no other FFA call from this VM can reach the SP before the VM creation message. Note that supporting the VM destruction message is more urgent than supporting the VM creation message so It might be useful to split this CL in two and handle the destruction case first.",
      "parentUuid": "feec5b27_002c75a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 384,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 384,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89e660cc_928d36dd",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 384,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-07T12:41:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. So it sounds like this should be moved to the VM finalisation code (on first run?).",
      "parentUuid": "146325ce_277ba84d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 384,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 384,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
