    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0163a976_ca9ced74",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-09T01:46:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not safe, but I\u0027m not sure how to handle an arbitrary SP count. Can we allocate anything in the hypervisor?",
      "parentUuid": "194ffc19_3f94a322",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1170,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 1170,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "be0dec8a_4dc50014",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-09T01:48:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One option could be to call `FFA_PARTITION_INFO_GET` before every message, but then how would we keep track of which SPs we have already notified?",
      "parentUuid": "0163a976_ca9ced74",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1170,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 1170,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "be55e088_35062364",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
