      },
      "lineNbr": 1170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-17T15:04:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I updated it to return `FFA_RET_NO_MEMORY` if we overflow the array.",
      "parentUuid": "be0dec8a_4dc50014",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1170,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 1170,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "050529f5_c6d975aa",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-08T04:18:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SPs can ask for one of the two messages but not the other, e.g., Trusty only cares about VM destruction. The check could be `!\u003d 0` to support that case.",
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea7cc69e_ef9a638e",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T15:34:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will relax this check to `!\u003d0`.",
      "parentUuid": "050529f5_c6d975aa",
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f44b200e_05a0ef0d",
