      "lineNbr": 1345,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-08T02:16:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the general sense, is `ret` here a kernel error code or an FF-A one? This function seems to mix them up.",
      "parentUuid": "6b9ff779_f397d435",
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b28ab055_2591ac5d",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1345,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T15:34:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good observation. Most FF-A codes are positive numbers but the caller of this function expects only : `ret \u003d\u003d 0` or `ret \u003d\u003d -EAGAIN` otherwise it explodes. \n\nThis is a place where the spec needs improvement IMO.  If Trustzone returns interrupted in response to the `FFA_VM_DESTRUCTION_MSG`, do we have a guarantee that this will complete in the near future in `x us` if we retry  ?",
      "parentUuid": "76bd1e2e_44abd243",
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "32da4dfb_9f08a441",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1345,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-19T02:39:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e do we have a guarantee that this will complete in the near future in x us if we retry ?\n\nNo, but afaik you don\u0027t have that guarantee if `FFA_VM_DESTRUCTION_MSG` is synchronous.\n\nRe the error code: I think `RETRY` makes more sense for regular asynchronous calls, `INTERRUPTED` usually means non-secure interrupts specifically.",
      "parentUuid": "b28ab055_2591ac5d",
      "revId": "0e31869112558cbf16eb0e153d2bc55c73443f68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
